  "title": "Patrick M NDE 3867",
  "date": "'August second, nineteen seventy-seven'",
  "content": "It was funny because I really did not think it was real. It was so unreal. I was listening to a voice while I was watching my family, my mother, sisters, and even my father were there. They were all standing around a hospital bed. About the same time, I am given a decision to make, to stay, or I could go with a couple of my close friends. At the same time, it was dawning on me and then the doctor was checking my eyes and the monitor is beeping and commotion. I was told that I had an accident and I was okay. That I had been working with a boom truck (small crane) they are telling me I scared everybody, that one minute I was over there touching the large metal box and then a loud SNAP and I was thrown about forty-fifty feet away. The truck tires exploded then the electricity went to ground through the truck stiff legs. My friend or coworker told me I scared everybody then, the CPR was not working, and then at one point I sat straight up my mouth wide open screaming but there was no sound. The audio was not working. Then I blacked out again.",
